@* The useful case on this stack: the server raises it. Ctx.UpEmit("flash:show", …) sends an
   X-Up-Events header, one line in ui.js turns it into a toast, and the handler that did the work
   is the thing that announces it — no flash cookie, no session state, no second request. *@
<form id="toast-from-server-form" method="post" action="/orders/3201/refund" up-target="#preview-toast-from-server" up-disable>
    <AntiforgeryToken />
    <Button Type="submit" Variant="outline">Refund — the server raises the toast</Button>
</form>

<pre data-slot="code-block-pre" class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md border bg-card p-3 text-[12.5px]"><code>// in the handler
Ctx.UpEmit("flash:show", new { text = "Refunded $248.00", kind = "success" });</code></pre>
